  "summary": "I added a \"Close portal\" button below the canvas in `src/main.ts`. `typecheck` passes and the render shows the button under the canvas with the portal open and no errors. I haven't clicked the button, so the close and reopen behaviour is untested.\n\nClicking it hides the vortex disc and both particle groups, turns the three portal lights off, and sets `window.__TASK_STATE__` to `portalActive: false` and `particleCount: 0`. The label changes to \"Open portal\". The state is updated at once and again every frame while closed.\n\nClicking again shows everything and the label goes back to \"Close portal\". `particleCount` returns to 330 and `portalActive` to true. While the portal is closed the camera keeps swaying, and the ring and runes stay visible. The rune slabs are unlit, so they keep their glow."
